description:
Menus, shortcuts and a command palette work best from one table of commands. Write it:

```cpp
struct Command
{
    std::string name;          // "File/Save"
    std::string shortcut;      // "Ctrl+S", or "" for none (already in a normal form: modifiers Ctrl, Shift, Alt in that order)
    std::function<bool()> enabled;    // may be empty: always enabled
    std::function<void()> run;
};

class Commands
{
public:
    void add(Command c);
    std::vector<std::string> clashes() const;          // "Ctrl+S: File/Save, Edit/Select" for each shortcut used twice or more
    bool press(const std::string& shortcut);            // run the command with this shortcut, if any is enabled
    std::vector<std::string> menu(const std::string& top) const;   // items under a top-level menu
};
```

- `clashes`: one line per shortcut used by two or more commands, in alphabetical order of shortcut; the command names in the order they were added, joined with `", "`.
- `press`: among commands with this shortcut, run the **first added one that is enabled** and return `true`; return `false` if none is enabled or none has it.
- `menu("File")`: for each command whose name starts with `File/`, in order added, the text after `File/`, followed by `"  "` and the shortcut if it has one, and ` (disabled)` if its `enabled` returns false right now.

